What lorekeeper holds the mystery to this relic, few can determine.  Scripts emblazed into the sides of this bow show that it is indeed derived from elvish ancestry, and that those that crafted it honored Ilsare with their work.

Bringing the bow to aim reveals a needle sized eyesight, it seems to be a thin strand of mithril that glows in it's center with a cross section of delicate threadlike strands of the metal.  It is impressive the illuminating power this eyesight holds.  The bowstring is attached strangely to the actual bow, and the string it self is burning to the hand if held for too long.  Small streams of fire can be seen at times spiralling downwards along the thin strand, and you imagine it must take some great degree of skill to maintain a quick and steady hand with this impressive relic.

// GM NOTE: The arrows produced from this bow are for the sole use of the bow's owner and are not to be traded or sold under any circumstances.

This pearlescent beverage seems to glow with an inner light.  A cursory sniff of its contents first sends the rush of alcohol through the sinuses, followed by an inexplicable feeling of well-being.

This was the prize provided by Matthew Callahan for the "Sacrifice" storyteller's night.

// Note: This beverage does not provide any of the RP restorative properties of Greater Restoration.  It merely restores hitpoints and removes negative effects.

This rod is presented to serving members of the Diet of Lor, the political body that serves the twin Mayors. It is a symbol of power to the people of Lor and demands support among all those who serve Lor.

// Target the ground to create a safe rest area, once/RL day.
// If in Lor or environs, can be used to send perpetrators to jail, summon help, or enforce the law.

